# unit-subset.list: the subset of unit-tests.list that the KVM suite's case
# unit-subset-nested runs on the host-svm profile, in that list's format, to
# set Rach2 beside Linux as the KVM host of the same machine: every test
# unit-tests.list runs but debug and xapic, which Linux 6.12 as that host did
# not finish in 900 s, debug after its MOVSS-blocking single step and xapic
# after nmi-after-sti. It runs in about half an hour under either host on
# the testing PC, 12 to 14 minutes of it x2apic's. EXPECT is
# unit-tests.list's. LINUX is the result of Debian's Linux 6.12.107 as the
# host of the same machine with an invariant TSC, run by linux-corpus.sh -k
# unit on 2026-11-12, and REASON names Linux's failure and skip where the
# two differ or Linux fails.
#
# NAME EXPECT LINUX REASON
access pass pass
access-reduced-maxphyaddr skip skip /sys/module/kvm_intel/parameters/allow_smaller_maxphyaddr not equal to Y
access_fep skip skip Forced emulation prefix (FEP) not available
cet skip skip No CET features supported
emulator pass pass
eventinj pass pass
hypercall pass pass
hyperv_clock pass pass
hyperv_connections fail fail Linux: receive pending message: 0/2, as Rach2
hyperv_stimer pass pass
hyperv_stimer_direct pass pass
hyperv_synic pass pass
idt_test pass pass
intel_iommu pass pass
ioapic pass pass
kvmclock_test pass pass
la57 pass fail Linux: la57.c:230: assert failed: write_cr4_safe(read_cr4() | X86_CR4_PCIDE) == 0, as Rach2
lam pass pass
memory pass pass
msr pass pass
msr64 pass pass
pcid-asymmetric pass pass
pcid-disabled pass fail Linux: FAIL: Test on INVPCID when disabled, as Rach2
pcid-enabled pass pass
pks skip skip PKS not enabled: the processor has no PKS
pku skip skip PKU not enabled
pmu kvm_pmu?hypervisor?fail:pass:skip fail Linux: 21 to 22 of 77 fail, the instruction counts 2 to 13% high, the six counters together and every overflow; skips without a host PMU
pmu_lbr kvm_lbr?pass:skip skip Linux's on the testing PC, which offers no LBR format; the Lenovo's Debian passes it with Haswell's 16 records
pmu_pebs skip skip Linux's on the testing PC; PEBS is not offered, and the Lenovo's Debian reference settles Intel's
rdpru pass pass
realmode pass pass
rmap_chain pass pass
s3 pass pass
setjmp pass pass
sieve pass pass
smap smap?pass:skip pass SMAP not enabled, on a processor without it, as the Lenovo's i3-4030U
smptest pass pass
smptest3 pass pass
syscall pass pass
tsc pass pass
tsc_adjust pass pass
tsx-ctrl skip skip TSX not available
umip pass pass
vmexit_cpuid pass pass
vmexit_cr0_wp pass pass
vmexit_cr4_pge pass pass
vmexit_inl_pmtimer pass pass
vmexit_ipi pass pass
vmexit_ipi_halt pass pass
vmexit_mov_from_cr8 pass pass
vmexit_mov_to_cr8 pass pass
vmexit_ple_round_robin pass pass
vmexit_tscdeadline pass pass
vmexit_tscdeadline_immed pass pass
vmexit_vmcall pass pass
vmware_backdoors skip skip /sys/module/kvm/parameters/enable_vmware_backdoor not equal to Y
x2apic pass fail Linux: nmi-after-sti fails, as under Rach2; TMCCT should not be reset to TMICT value passed in each of the 3 Linux runs kept and in 1 of 4 Rach2 runs, as a report line between its two reads spans several timer periods there; the test takes 640 to 849 s
xsave pass pass
